---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Converter from '../components/Converter';
import { LIMITS, formatBytes } from '../config/limits';
const faqs = [
  ['Are my images uploaded?', 'No. Your browser reads and converts the files on your device. Images and filenames are not sent to a server or stored by this tool. Closing or reloading this page clears the queue.'],
  ['How do I convert multiple WebP files?', 'Choose or drop up to 10 images, then select Convert to PNG. The queue processes one image at a time. Download individual PNGs, or use Download all (.zip) for the successful results.'],
  ['Will my transparent background stay transparent?', 'Yes. Transparent pixels are kept when a static WebP image is drawn to the canvas and exported to PNG. The converter does not add a white background.'],
  ['Why is my PNG file larger?', 'PNG and WebP compress images differently. PNG may be much larger, especially when the original WebP uses lossy compression. Conversion does not recover detail already lost in the original image.'],
  ['Can I convert animated WebP?', 'No. This version supports static WebP only. Animated files are identified from the WebP container and rejected; the converter does not silently save the first frame.'],
  ['What are the file limits?', `The queue accepts up to ${LIMITS.files} images, each up to ${formatBytes(LIMITS.inputBytes)} and ${LIMITS.pixels / 1_000_000} megapixels. Completed PNGs can total up to ${formatBytes(LIMITS.resultBytes)}; ZIP downloads accept up to ${formatBytes(LIMITS.zipBytes)} of PNGs. These are this tool’s safeguards. MB means 1,000,000 bytes.`],
  ['What should I do if a conversion fails?', 'Read the message beside the file. Check that it is a complete, static WebP image within the limits, or export it again from the original app. Free memory or remove completed results, then select Retry. A failed file does not stop the others.'],
];
---
<Layout title="WebP to PNG Converter – Free & No Upload" description="Convert WebP to PNG for free in your browser. Keep transparent backgrounds, convert up to 10 static images, and download PNG or ZIP. No upload or signup.">
  <section class="hero"><h1>WebP to PNG Converter</h1><p>A PNG when you need one. Free, local to your browser, and no signup.</p></section>
  <noscript><style>.converter { display: none !important; }</style><p class="noscript">This converter needs JavaScript to process images in your browser. Enable JavaScript and reload to choose files. The guide and information below are still available.</p></noscript>
  <Converter client:load />
  <section class="how-section" aria-labelledby="how-title"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="how-title">From WebP to PNG in three steps.</h2><a href="/guides/convert-webp-to-png/">Read the illustrated guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="steps">
    <div class="step"><span class="step-num">1</span><div><h3>Choose your images</h3><p>Drop WebP files above or select them from your device.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="step-num">2</span><div><h3>Make the conversion</h3><p>Click Convert to PNG. Your browser does the work locally.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><span class="step-num">3</span><div><h3>Save your PNGs</h3><p>Download one at a time, or take them together in a ZIP.</p></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="feature-section"><div><h2>Your image. A different format.</h2><p>Keep the original width, height, and transparent areas. Get a real PNG for apps and workflows that need one, without sending your image away.</p><p>Conversion does not improve image quality, promise a smaller file, or preserve every piece of metadata. Your original file stays untouched.</p></div><div><h2>A few practical limits.</h2><ul class="limits-list"><li><span>Input format</span><strong>Static WebP</strong></li><li><span>Queue size</span><strong>{LIMITS.files} images</strong></li><li><span>Per image</span><strong>{formatBytes(LIMITS.inputBytes)} · {LIMITS.pixels / 1_000_000} MP</strong></li><li><span>Result cache / ZIP input</span><strong>{formatBytes(LIMITS.resultBytes)} / {formatBytes(LIMITS.zipBytes)}</strong></li></ul><p>Limits help manage browser memory. Download and remove finished images to make room.</p></div></section>
  <section class="faq-section"><div><h2>Good to know.</h2><p>A few answers before you convert.</p></div><div>{faqs.map(([question, answer]) => <details><summary>{question}</summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div></section>
</Layout>
